.TH DASHBOARD-CLI 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dashboard-cli \- console-style session on the dashboard control server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dashboard-cli
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
A session front-end on top of the dashboard's JSON-lines control socket:
prompt with the connected port, TAB completion and \fB?\fR in every
position (with the short descriptions from the shared command registry),
\fBset\fR commands print only the confirmation, \fBshow <setting>\fR
prints the bare value, \fBshow status\fR the key=value report, and
\fBshutdown\fR asks before it stops the server. When the connection dies
mid-session the console
retries (\fB--reconnect\fR attempts, \fB--reconnect-wait\fR seconds
apart). With a control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: the
console signs every command and verifies every reply.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (default: /tmp/dashboard\-8080.socket; env CTL when
unset) — same flag as the server itself
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds (default 5.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect " N"
when the connection dies (an unanswered ping, a reset, a timeout), retry
this many times before giving up; 0 = off (default 3)
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect\-wait " N"
seconds between the reconnect attempts (default 10.0)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token\-file
the token from a file (the first line; must be owner\-only 0600); not
for use with \-\-control\-token (env CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout; default: the XDG state home
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size in MB, keeping 3 backups; 0 = off
(default 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail (default: off)


.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTL
the default control target for the clients.
.TP
.B CONTROL_TOKEN ", " CLI_KEEPALIVE
the TCP token and the idle-ping interval in seconds (0 = off).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dashboard-ctl (1),
.BR dashboard (1)
